,477 × 50,000,000 equals 4,773,850,000,000, and then I need to carefully compute 95,477 × 1,169,614 by further decomposing it into 95,477 × 1,000,000 plus 95,477 × 169,614. For the remaining piece, I'll express 169,614 as 170,000 minus 386 to simplify the multiplication.\n\nWorking through the final calculations: 95,477 × 170,000 gives 16,231,090,000, and 95,477 × 386 breaks down to 38,190,800 minus 1,336,678, which equals 36,854,122. Subtracting these yields 95,477 × 169,614 = 16,194,235,878. Adding back the million-unit component: 95,477 × 1,169,614 = 111,671,235,878. The complete product is 4,885,521,235,878.\n\nThe remainder when dividing 4,885,521,246,185 by this product is 10,307, which is less than 95,477, confirming the quotient is 51,169,614. I notice my initial calculation had a different result, so this verification is important. but I made an error in my first attempt. Let me recalculate to see where I went wrong.\n\nI initially computed 95477 × 52,169,614 and got 4,885,522,190,648, which exceeds the target. The difference between 52,169,614 and 51,169,614 is exactly 1,000,000, so multiplying by 95,477 gives 95,477,000,000. This confirms that 52,169,614 is too large. I had a typo where I wrote \"52\" instead of \"51\" in the quotient. The correct answer is 51,169,614. Verifying: 95477 × 51,169,614 = 4,885,521,235,878, which is less than 4,885,521,246,185, and 95477 × 51,169,615 = 4,885,521,331,355, which exceeds it. So the floor is 51,169,614.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":18944,"cache_read_input_tokens":20965,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":18944},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"03c72ba8-d605-e770-8a63-f881ffd0f9d5","uuid":"f0d65bc1-f72f-41e1-bbc9-d49febfd812b"}
